Project: event analytics platform for Kamel Ride, a student ride-share
social app. Built as a take-home for a product engineering internship.

Stack (do not substitute):
- TypeScript strict mode everywhere, ES modules
- Backend: Fastify, deployed as Vercel serverless functions
- Validation: Zod
- DB: Postgres on Neon, via the `postgres` (postgres.js) package
- Frontend: Vite + React + Recharts
- npm workspaces monorepo: packages/shared, packages/server,
  packages/web, packages/simulator

Rules:
- Event types and Zod schemas live in packages/shared and are imported by
  every other package. Never redefine a type locally.
- No `any`. No non-null assertions.
- Serverless constraints: no in-memory state between requests, no
  WebSockets, no local file writes. Use a pooled Neon connection.
- Env vars are Zod-parsed once in a config module at startup; never read
  process.env elsewhere.
- Every file gets a one-line header comment explaining its role.
- Explain choices in comments where a reviewer would ask "why this and
  not the obvious alternative?"

Workflow:
- The repo root, git, .gitignore, .env and workspace layout already exist.
  Do not run git init, do not create commits, do not restructure folders.
